1. Wireshark Basics

Start Wireshark

wireshark

List available capture interfaces:

tshark -D

Capture packets on a specific interface:

sudo tshark -i eth0

Save packets to a capture file:

sudo tshark -i eth0 -w network-capture.pcapng

Read a saved capture:

wireshark network-capture.pcapng

Read it from the terminal:

tshark -r network-capture.pcapng

Replace "eth0" with your actual interface, which you can find using:

ip -br addr

Essential Wireshark interface features

Feature| Purpose
Display Filter bar| Filter captured packets
Packet List| View packets and their summary information
Packet Details| Expand protocol fields for a selected packet
Packet Bytes| Inspect raw packet bytes in hexadecimal and ASCII
Follow Stream| Reconstruct a conversation between endpoints
Expert Information| Review protocol warnings and unusual conditions
Conversations| Summarize communication between endpoints
Endpoints| List hosts and other endpoints seen in the capture
I/O Graphs| Visualize traffic volume and patterns

