6. HTTP and Web Traffic Analysis

6.1 Inspect HTTP requests

Use:

http.request

Expand Hypertext Transfer Protocol to inspect:

- Request method
- Host header
- Request URI
- User-Agent
- Content-Type
- Content-Length
- Cookies, if present in unencrypted traffic

6.2 Inspect HTTP responses

Use:

http.response

Inspect:

- Status code
- Server header, if present
- Content-Type
- Content-Length
- Redirect headers
- Response body, when available

6.3 Find POST requests

http.request.method == "POST"
POST requests are not inherently malicious. Inspect their context, destination, headers, and content when it is appropriate to do so.

6.4 Export HTTP objects

When a supported HTTP object is present in the capture:

1. Open File → Export Objects → HTTP.
2. Review the listed objects.
3. Select an object.
4. Export it to a controlled analysis directory.
5. Inspect the file safely before opening or executing it.

Not every capture contains exportable objects. Encrypted HTTPS payloads cannot normally be exported as readable HTTP objects without successful decryption.

